https://api.github.com/users/andrej-petrovic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrej-petrovic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Actually, upon closer inspection, it is not true that the signal is \"Emitted when ColroPicker.color is changed\". A user could do something like:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\ncolor_picker_button.get_picker().color = Color( ... )\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis calls the picker's `set_pick_color` method directly, which doesn't emit `ColorPicker.color_changed` and so `ColorPickerButton.color_changed` won't get called either.\r\n\r\nThe most accurate phrasing would be something like:\r\n\r\n> Emitted when the underlying ColorPicker's color_changed signal is emitted, or when the user closes the modal using `ui_cancel`.\r\n\r\nBut that's horribly verbose and that whole modal closing thing needlessly complicates it. Not really sure what the best approach is. Starting to think that  \"changed by the user\" might be the more concise way of phrasing it, as long as it's actually true...","created_at":"2025-05-03T19:40:29Z","updated_at":"2025-05-03T19:40:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106054#discussion_r2072454057","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106054","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2072454057"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106054#discussion_r2072454057"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106054"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2072454057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":45,"original_line":45,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2072438552,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":13,"position":